  "notation": "Own notation: 0,(3), 0,1(6); comma decimal separator, parentheses mark the period. No Casio skin or original-output claim.",
  "componentMeaning": "sign is -1/0/1; integerPart is unsigned; preperiod and period are digit strings (empty period means finite). Components and unlimitedText describe the exact expansion even when bounded planned output falls back or fails.",
  "budgetContract": "Generated digits count preperiod plus one complete minimal period, or finite fractional digits. Integer digits, sign, comma and parentheses do not consume this digit budget. Zero budget allows integers only. Exceeding it plans canonical reduced-fraction fallback expansionLimit. Character budget then covers the entire chosen text, including sign, comma, both parentheses or fraction slash; exceeding it plans limit (no second fallback). expectedFallback records the selected fallback reason even when its text exceeds the character budget; expectedText and expectedFormat are then null.",
  "oracle": "Closed form sign * (integerPart + preperiodInteger/10^m + periodInteger/[10^m*(10^n-1)]), omitting empty terms; verified by Python fractions.Fraction. Digits are supplied independently, not calculated by long division or product code.",
